<title>USA: US banks free rsrvs $724 mln/day April 9 two wks.</title>
<headline>US banks free rsrvs $724 mln/day April 9 two wks.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. commercial banks had free reserves of $724 million per day in the two weeks ended April 9, versus revised free reserves of $887 million in the previous two-week period, the Federal Reserve said.</p>
<p>Seasonal borrowings were $61 million versus $38 million a day. Extended credits were nil.</p>
<p>((-- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660))</p>
</text>
